The Tailcat tailnet nodes in tailcat/native and tailcat/host build against Go modules
downloaded at build time, among them github.com/tailscale/tailcat (BSD-3-Clause). Each
module keeps the license it ships with.

The Japanese flick, pinyin and Zhuyin packages in ios/InputMethods keep their upstream
licenses and notices beside their code and data:
- McBopomofo (MIT): ios/InputMethods/McBopomofoEngine.
- The Zhuyin data, from libtabe (BSD), and McBopomofo: ZhuyinInput/Sources/ZhuyinInput/Resources/Notices.
- The pinyin dictionary, derived from rime-wanxiang (https://github.com/amzxyz/rime-wanxiang,
  CC-BY-4.0) and modified: PinyinInput/Sources/PinyinInput/Resources/Notices.
- The Japanese dictionary from azooKey (Apache-2.0), AzooKeyKanaKanjiConverter and Jinja (MIT)
  and the Swift packages they use (Apache-2.0): JapaneseInput/Sources/JapaneseInput/Resources/Notices.
